  "finding": "Within a single configuration, 20-34 of 210 pairwise verdicts change winner from seed to seed. Median-of-five is the right magnitude estimator, but a pairwise VERDICT whose median margin is below the seed noise is decided by the seed, not by the formats. Unstable verdicts here reach median margins of up to ~30%, so 'A is faster than B' at margins under that is not established by five seeds of one configuration. This is the project's own three-seed rule (a silicon verdict must agree across placer seeds) applied to throughput comparisons."
